	{{block('/-/block/find_a_location___cta_box___ja.html?variant=7-f6df82c797-p4mfwk')}}
	<div style="background-color:#FFFFFF;" classname="{styles.pvlRow}" class="row mt-16 mb-16 top-8">
		<div style="flex:1" className={styles.pvlColumn}>
			<div class="container my-5">
        <h2 class="mb-4">Food Pantry FAQs</h2>
        
        <div class="accordion faq-section" id="faqAccordion">
            
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem1" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: How do I find a Salvation Army food pantry near me?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: Use the food pantry locator at the top of this page to search by ZIP code. The locator can help you find the nearest Salvation Army location, hours, and contact information. Mobile pantry schedules may change, so it is best to call ahead.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem2" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: Do I need an appointment to visit a food pantry?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: Many Salvation Army food pantries welcome walk-ins during scheduled hours. Some high-demand locations may ask clients to call ahead or make an appointment. Contact your nearest location before your first visit to confirm hours and requirements.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem3" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: How often can I visit a Salvation Army food pantry?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: Visit frequency varies by location. Some pantries allow weekly visits, while others may provide assistance monthly. If you need more help than one visit provides, Salvation Army staff may be able to connect you with additional resources.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem4" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: Is food assistance free?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: Yes. Salvation Army food pantry services, mobile pantry distributions, food parcels, and community meals are free. There is no cost, no suggested donation, and no requirement to attend a religious service.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem5" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: Do I have to be Christian to receive food from The Salvation Army?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: No. The Salvation Army is a Christian organization, but food assistance is available to people in need regardless of faith, background, or belief. There is no requirement to attend church, participate in prayer, or take part in religious programming to receive food assistance.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem6" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: Do I need to show proof of income?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: Most Salvation Army food programs do not require proof of income. Some locations may request basic information because of local program rules or federal food assistance guidelines. Contact your nearest location to confirm what is needed.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem7" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: Do I need proof of immigration status?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem7" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: Most Salvation Army locations do not require proof of immigration status to receive food assistance. Where identification is requested, locations may accept several forms of ID. Many locations can also assist people who do not have documentation.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem8" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: Can I receive food if I already get SNAP or WIC?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem8" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: Yes. People who receive SNAP, WIC, or other benefits may still use a Salvation Army food pantry. Pantry assistance and federal nutrition benefits are designed to work together. Many households still face food gaps even when they receive benefits.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem9" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: Can someone pick up food for me?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem9" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: At many locations, yes. A caregiver, family member, or approved proxy may be able to pick up food for someone who is homebound or unable to travel. Call the pantry before pickup to ask what information is required.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem10" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: What kinds of food are available?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem10" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: Food varies by location and supply. Many pantries provide shelf-stable groceries, protein items, bread, dairy or dairy alternatives, and fresh produce when available. Some locations also offer diapers, hygiene products, or household essentials.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem11" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: Can Salvation Army food pantries accommodate special diets?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem11" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: Client-choice pantries are often better able to support dietary needs because clients can select the foods that work for their household. At traditional pantries, let staff know if you have dietary needs such as vegetarian, low-sodium, halal, kosher, allergy-related, or medically necessary restrictions. Availability varies by location.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem12" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: What is a mobile food pantry?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem12" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: A mobile food pantry is a scheduled food distribution that brings groceries to communities without easy access to a fixed pantry. Mobile pantries may serve rural areas, food deserts, disaster zones, or neighborhoods where transportation is a barrier.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem13" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: How does The Salvation Army fight hunger beyond food pantries?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem13" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: The Salvation Army fights hunger through neighborhood pantries, client-choice pantries, mobile food distributions, food parcel delivery, community kitchens, hot meal routes, disaster feeding, SNAP assistance, and benefits navigation. Across these programs, the mission is the same: to serve people who are hungry with dignity, practical help, and compassion.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem14" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: What can I donate to a food pantry?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem14" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: Most food pantries need shelf-stable, unopened foods that are easy to store and prepare. Helpful donations often include canned proteins, peanut butter, pasta, rice, cereal, canned fruits, canned vegetables, soup, shelf-stable milk, baby food, and formula. Many locations also need non-food essentials such as diapers, wipes, hygiene products, toilet paper, cleaning supplies, and laundry detergent. Before donating, check with your nearest Salvation Army location. Needs vary by community, and some pantries may have specific guidelines for refrigerated items, fresh produce, expired food, or bulk donations.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
            <div class="accordion-item faq-item">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqItem15" aria-expanded="false">
                        <span class="faq-question"><strong>Q: What is a food desert?</strong></span>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="faqItem15" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <span class="faq-answer">A: A food desert is an area where people have limited access to affordable, nutritious food. This can happen in rural communities with few nearby grocery stores or in urban neighborhoods where residents may not have reliable transportation to reach fresh food. In food deserts, families may rely more heavily on convenience stores, gas stations, or fast food because those are the closest available options. Mobile food pantries help by bringing groceries directly into communities where access to healthy food is limited.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
 
        </div>
    </div>
 
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
